DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The   uunnggeettwwcc()  function  is  the  wide‐character  equivalent  of  the
       uunnggeettcc(3) function.  It pushes back a wide character  onto  _s_t_r_e_a_m  and
       returns it.

       If _w_c is WWEEOOFF, it returns WWEEOOFF.  If _w_c is an invalid wide character, it
       sets _e_r_r_n_o to EEIILLSSEEQQ and returns WWEEOOFF.

       If  _w_c is a valid wide character, it is pushed back onto the stream and
       thus becomes available for future wide‐character read operations.   The
       file‐position indicator is decremented by one or more.  The end‐of‐file
       indicator is cleared.  The backing storage of the file is not affected.

       Note:  _w_c  need not be the last wide‐character read from the stream; it
       can be any other valid wide character.

       If the implementation supports multiple push‐back operations in a  row,
       the pushed‐back wide characters will be read in reverse order; however,
       only one level of push‐back is guaranteed.

